    "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><title>Spicy Tteokbokki | Example Kitchen</title><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@graph\": [{\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"Example Kitchen\"}, {\"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": []}, {\"@type\": \"Recipe\", \"name\": \"Spicy Tteokbokki\", \"description\": \"Chewy rice cakes in a sweet and fiery sauce.\", \"recipeYield\": \"2\", \"totalTime\": \"PT25M\", \"recipeIngredient\": [\"500 g Korean rice cakes (tteok)\", \"2 tbsp gochujang\", \"1 tbsp soy sauce\", \"1 tbsp sugar\", \"2 spring onions, cut into 5 cm lengths\", \"500 ml water\", \"2 garlic cloves, minced\"], \"recipeInstructions\": [{\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"text\": \"Bring the water to the boil with the gochujang, soy sauce, sugar and garlic.\"}, {\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"text\": \"Add the rice cakes and simmer for 10-12 minutes, stirring, until the sauce thickens.\"}, {\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"text\": \"Stir in the spring onions and serve hot.\"}], \"image\": [\"https://example.com/photo.jpg\"], \"author\": {\"@type\": \"Person\", \"name\": \"Jo\"}, \"aggregateRating\": {\"@type\": \"AggregateRating\", \"ratingValue\": \"4.8\"}}]}</script></head><body><header><nav><a href='/'>Home</a> <a href='/recipes'>Recipes</a> <a href='/about'>About</a></nav></header><div class='ad'>ADVERTISEMENT - Subscribe to our newsletter!</div><article><h1>Spicy Tteokbokki</h1><p>Chewy rice cakes in a sweet and fiery sauce.</p><p>There is something about this dish that takes me straight back to my grandmother&#x27;s kitchen. Before we get to it, a word from our sponsor: 20% off cast-iron pans this week! I have made this more times than I can count, tweaking it over the years.</p><p class='meta'>2</p><h2>Ingredients</h2><ul><li>500 g Korean rice cakes (tteok)</li><li>2 tbsp gochujang</li><li>1 tbsp soy sauce</li><li>1 tbsp sugar</li><li>2 spring onions, cut into 5 cm lengths</li><li>500 ml water</li><li>2 garlic cloves, minced</li></ul><div class='ad'>ADVERTISEMENT</div><h2>Method</h2><ol><li>Bring the water to the boil with the gochujang, soy sauce, sugar and garlic.</li><li>Add the rice cakes and simmer for 10-12 minutes, stirring, until the sauce thickens.</li><li>Stir in the spring onions and serve hot.</li></ol></article><section class='comments'><h3>Comments</h3><p>Made this tonight, loved it! - Sam</p></section><footer>© Example Kitchen. Privacy. Cookies.</footer></body></html>",
