    "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><title>Weeknight Chicken Curry | Example Kitchen</title><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"Recipe\", \"name\": \"Weeknight Chicken Curry\", \"description\": \"A mild, creamy curry.\", \"recipeYield\": \"Serves 4\", \"prepTime\": \"PT15M\", \"cookTime\": \"PT35M\", \"recipeIngredient\": [\"600 g boneless, skinless chicken thighs, diced\", \"1 large onion, chopped\", \"3 cloves garlic, grated\", \"thumb-sized piece of ginger, grated\", \"2 tbsp medium curry powder\", \"400 ml can coconut milk\", \"1 tbsp vegetable oil\", \"a handful of fresh coriander\"], \"recipeInstructions\": [{\"@type\": \"HowToSection\", \"name\": \"Prepare\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"text\": \"Fry the onion in the oil for 8 minutes.\"}, {\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"text\": \"Add the garlic, ginger and curry powder.\"}]}, {\"@type\": \"HowToSection\", \"name\": \"Cook\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"text\": \"Add the chicken and brown it.\"}, {\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"text\": \"Pour in the coconut milk and simmer 25 minutes.\"}, {\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"text\": \"Scatter with coriander.\"}]}], \"image\": [\"https://example.com/photo.jpg\"], \"author\": {\"@type\": \"Person\", \"name\": \"Jo\"}, \"aggregateRating\": {\"@type\": \"AggregateRating\", \"ratingValue\": \"4.8\"}}</script></head><body><header><nav><a href='/'>Home</a> <a href='/recipes'>Recipes</a> <a href='/about'>About</a></nav></header><div class='ad'>ADVERTISEMENT - Subscribe to our newsletter!</div><article><h1>Weeknight Chicken Curry</h1><p>A mild, creamy curry.</p><p>There is something about this dish that takes me straight back to my grandmother&#x27;s kitchen. Before we get to it, a word from our sponsor: 20% off cast-iron pans this week! I have made this more times than I can count, tweaking it over the years.</p><p class='meta'>Serves 4</p><h2>Ingredients</h2><ul><li>600 g boneless, skinless chicken thighs, diced</li><li>1 large onion, chopped</li><li>3 cloves garlic, grated</li><li>thumb-sized piece of ginger, grated</li><li>2 tbsp medium curry powder</li><li>400 ml can coconut milk</li><li>1 tbsp vegetable oil</li><li>a handful of fresh coriander</li></ul><div class='ad'>ADVERTISEMENT</div><h2>Method</h2><ol><li>Fry the onion in the oil for 8 minutes.</li><li>Add the garlic, ginger and curry powder.</li><li>Add the chicken and brown it.</li><li>Pour in the coconut milk and simmer 25 minutes.</li><li>Scatter with coriander.</li></ol></article><section class='comments'><h3>Comments</h3><p>Made this tonight, loved it! - Sam</p></section><footer>© Example Kitchen. Privacy. Cookies.</footer></body></html>",
