    "html": "<!doctype html><html><head><title>Smoky Shakshuka | Example Kitchen</title></head><body><header><nav><a href='/'>Home</a> <a href='/recipes'>Recipes</a> <a href='/about'>About</a></nav></header><div class='ad'>ADVERTISEMENT - Subscribe to our newsletter!</div><article><h1>Smoky Shakshuka</h1><p></p><p>There is something about this dish that takes me straight back to my grandmother&#x27;s kitchen. Before we get to it, a word from our sponsor: 20% off cast-iron pans this week! I have made this more times than I can count, tweaking it over the years.</p><p class='meta'>Serves 2 · Ready in 30 minutes</p><h2>Ingredients</h2><ul><li>2 tbsp olive oil</li><li>1 onion, diced</li><li>1 red pepper, sliced</li><li>2 garlic cloves, crushed</li><li>1 tsp ground cumin</li><li>1 tsp smoked paprika</li><li>2 x 400 g cans chopped tomatoes</li><li>4 eggs</li><li>50 g feta, crumbled</li><li>small bunch of parsley, chopped</li></ul><div class='ad'>ADVERTISEMENT</div><h2>Method</h2><ol><li>Soften the onion and pepper in the oil for 10 minutes.</li><li>Add the garlic and spices, then the tomatoes; simmer 10 minutes.</li><li>Make four wells, crack in the eggs, cover and cook 6-8 minutes.</li><li>Scatter with feta and parsley.</li></ol></article><section class='comments'><h3>Comments</h3><p>Made this tonight, loved it! - Sam</p></section><footer>© Example Kitchen. Privacy. Cookies.</footer></body></html>",
